      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, thanks. It's professional. \n\nHowever, I just checked the draft against our sentiment tool and the score came back a bit lower than I'd like for a \"recovery\" post—it's sitting at about a 0.62. My boss is a bit of a stickler for these metrics and he's worried that if the score isn't higher, the overall brand perception will continue to dip.\n\nCan you try a version that's a bit more uplifting and positive? I still need it to be an apology, but let's try to shift the tone so it feels more \"solution-oriented\" and bright. Just please, don't go overboard or make it look like we're laughing at them—I really don't want it to look fake, I just need that score to move up toward the 0.85 range.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
